---
import CaseStudyLayout from '../../layouts/CaseStudyLayout.astro';
import ProjectVisual from '../../components/ProjectVisual.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../consts';

const sections = [
  { id: 'overview', label: 'Overview' },
  { id: 'architecture', label: 'Architecture' },
  { id: 'rules', label: 'Decision engine' },
  { id: 'privacy', label: 'Privacy & safety' },
  { id: 'evidence', label: 'Evidence' },
  { id: 'limits', label: 'Limits & next' },
];
---

<CaseStudyLayout
  title="Guardian-Eye"
  subtitle="A multi-modal emergency detector that treats false positives as a design problem, not an inconvenience."
  kicker="Case study / Real-time detection"
  description="Guardian-Eye combines YOLOv8 pose estimation, gesture recognition, keyword spotting, and timed sensor fusion to detect emergencies and alert contacts through multiple channels."
  meta={[
    { label: 'Role', value: 'Engine, decision logic, dashboard' },
    { label: 'Timeline', value: '2026' },
    { label: 'Stack', value: 'Python · React · YOLOv8 · Firebase' },
    { label: 'Status', value: 'Active build · MIT' },
  ]}
  sections={sections}
  repoUrl={`${SITE.githubUrl}/Guardian-Eye`}
  outcomes={[
    { value: '3', label: 'signal sources' },
    { value: '5', label: 'timed rules' },
    { value: '3', label: 'alert channels' },
    { value: '1', label: 'live dashboard' },
  ]}
>
  <ProjectVisual slot="visual" slug="guardian-eye" />

  <section id="overview" class="article-section">
    <h2>Overview</h2>
    <p>
      A camera-only fall detector is easy to demo and hard to trust. A person sits down
      quickly, a chair occludes a limb, or the lighting changes — and the system calls for
      help. The opposite failure is worse: a real fall is missed because one signal was
      ambiguous.
    </p>
    <p>
      Guardian-Eye explores a different design. Three independent signals — vision, gesture,
      and voice — feed a timed decision engine. An alert requires persistence or agreement
      between signals, and the result is delivered through more than one channel.
    </p>
    <div class="article-callout">
      <strong>Design goal</strong>
      Keep inference local, make false positives expensive, and make a real emergency hard
      to miss. This is a safety tool, not a medical device.
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="architecture" class="article-section">
    <h2>Architecture</h2>
    <p>
      The edge engine runs on a Raspberry Pi, laptop, or desktop. Python's
      <code>multiprocessing</code> keeps video inference and audio listening from blocking
      each other. The browser dashboard is a separate React application in the same
      repository.
    </p>
    <div class="article-code">
      <span class="c"># signal path</span><br />
      Camera&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;→ YOLOv8 pose + gesture&nbsp;&nbsp;┐<br />
      &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;├→ Decision engine → Firebase<br />
      Microphone → Vosk / Google Speech&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;┘&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;→ Telegram<br />
      &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;→ GSM SMS
    </div>
    <p>
      Vision runs on-device. English keyword spotting uses Vosk locally. Malayalam
      recognition uses Google Speech when connectivity is available — an explicit
      trade-off between coverage and privacy.
    </p>
    <p>
      The dashboard shows a full-screen alert while it is open, but it is not the only
      delivery path. Telegram and the optional SIM800L GSM module are the out-of-app
      channels.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="rules" class="article-section">
    <h2>Decision engine</h2>
    <p>
      The engine combines the streams with timed state-machine rules. The first matching
      rule wins. Persistence is the main false-positive guard: a fall has to remain a fall.
    </p>
    <div class="article-table-wrap">
      <table class="article-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Condition</th>
            <th>Alert reason</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Fall persists for ≥ 10 seconds</td>
            <td>Fall detected for ≥ 10 seconds</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Fall ≥ 5 seconds plus a voice keyword</td>
            <td>Fall ≥ 5 seconds + voice emergency keyword</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>3 voice keywords within 20 seconds</td>
            <td>Voice emergency keyword repeated ≥ 3 times within 20 seconds</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Hand on chest for ≥ 10 seconds</td>
            <td>Hand on chest detected for ≥ 10 seconds</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Hand on chest plus a voice keyword</td>
            <td>Hand on chest + voice emergency keyword</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      The rules are deliberately conservative. A single frame, a single word, or a single
      gesture is not enough. The trade-off is latency: a real emergency may take a few
      seconds longer to confirm.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="privacy" class="article-section">
    <h2>Privacy & safety</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Local by default.</strong> Vision and English audio inference run on-device.
        Continuous video is not uploaded to a cloud service.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Explicit cloud boundary.</strong> Malayalam recognition sends audio to
        Google Speech when online. That boundary is documented rather than hidden.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Authenticated dashboard.</strong> Firebase access is governed by rules in
        the repository; the dashboard is not an open endpoint.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Multiple channels.</strong> A closed browser tab should not be the reason an
        alert is lost. Telegram and GSM provide independent paths.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>No clinical claim.</strong> The system is not a medical device and does not
        replace emergency services. It is designed to augment a care plan, not certify one.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <div class="article-callout">
      <strong>Safety note</strong>
      Any real deployment needs informed consent, a clear escalation path, and testing with
      the people who will actually use it. A demo is not a deployment.
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="evidence" class="article-section">
    <h2>Evidence</h2>
    <p>
      The repository contains the edge engine, the decision rules, the React dashboard, the
      Firebase rules, the demo mode, and setup instructions for a Raspberry Pi. The README
      documents the architecture and the exact alert conditions.
    </p>
    <p>
      The most important engineering evidence is the rule design: three noisy signals are
      combined in a way that can be explained, tested, and tuned. That is more useful than
      a single accuracy number without a dataset behind it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="limits" class="article-section">
    <h2>Limits & next</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Vision is sensitive to the scene.</strong> Lighting, occlusion, camera angle,
        and unusual body positions can produce false negatives or false positives.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Malayalam needs connectivity.</strong> The cloud path improves coverage but
        changes the privacy model.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>GSM is hardware-dependent.</strong> SMS delivery depends on the module,
        carrier, and signal. It is a fallback, not a guarantee.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>No clinical validation.</strong> The system has not been evaluated against a
        diverse, labeled dataset or in a clinical study.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Resource constraints.</strong> Continuous inference on a Raspberry Pi needs
        thermal and battery testing before long-term use.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Next: on-device Malayalam recognition, a more diverse test set, alert acknowledgment
      and escalation, and privacy-preserving performance metrics.
    </p>
  </section>
</CaseStudyLayout>
